{
  "dom_id": "step-q26148",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3.5a-4.5b-8=0 \\\\ 0.6a-1.2b-1.8=0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply both equations by $10,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3.5a-4.5b-8=0 & |\\,\\times 10 \\\\ 0.6a-1.2b-1.8=0 & |\\,\\times 10\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}35a-45b-80=0 \\\\ 6a-12b-18=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we can solve for $a$ in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6a-12b-18 & =0 \\\\ 6a & =12b+18 \\\\ a & =\\frac{12b+18}{6} \\\\ a & =2b+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the value of $b,$ we can substitute $a=2b+3$ into the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}35a-45b-80 & =0 \\\\ 35(2b+3)-45b-80 & =0 \\\\ 70b+105-45b-80 & =0 \\\\ 25b+25 & =0 \\\\ 25b & =-25 \\\\ b & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $b=-1$ into the equation $a=2b+3$ to get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =2b+3 \\\\ a & =2(-1)+3 \\\\ a & =-2+3 \\\\ a & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=1,\\,b=-1.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
